  "_why": {
   "no-storyboard": "the archetype IS the plan. A specimen shows one mechanism and has no beats to storyboard: engine-doctrine/CRAFT/SPECIMEN.md carries the decisions once, for the series.",
   "no-preflight": "the nine decisions are made in the scaffold, once, for every specimen. Making them again per demo is how each demo ends up looking like a different film.",
   "slow-pace": "a specimen is held on purpose. The pace floor grades films that must carry a story across their runtime; this one has one thing in it and you are meant to look at it.",
